WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.162
A force field does work only through the component aligned with movement

00:00:05.162 --> 00:00:08.733
A line integral adds that contribution along a path

00:00:08.733 --> 00:00:17.067
For the constant rightward field of magnitude one, moving from negative two to positive two along the axis gives work four.

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:24.267
On a counterclockwise circle of radius two, the rotational field matches the direction of motion

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:28.593
Both the field vector and the parametrization's derivative have length two

00:00:28.593 --> 00:00:34.100
Their dot product is four throughout the trip, so the work is eight pi.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:41.589
For the radial field on that same circle, every field arrow is perpendicular to the tangent direction

00:00:41.589 --> 00:00:49.233
The dot product is zero at every point, so the line integral vanishes even though the field itself is not zero.

00:00:50.533 --> 00:00:57.733
Reversing a path reverses the direction of each displacement, so a vector line integral changes sign

00:00:57.733 --> 00:01:01.783
This orientation rule differs from merely measuring path length

00:01:01.783 --> 00:01:07.633
Always specify the direction and distinguish work from a scalar integral against distance.
